WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.580
The Bible speaks of the Lord as the
Creator of heaven, earth and humanity.

00:00:06.580 --> 00:00:11.720
When it speaks of us, the focus
is not our hair or our eyes,

00:00:11.720 --> 00:00:15.520
our IQ or our emotional intelligence. No.

00:00:15.520 --> 00:00:21.820
It speaks of the Lord who forms
the human spirit within us.

00:00:21.820 --> 00:00:25.260
There is a spirit within each of us.

00:00:25.260 --> 00:00:28.040
The human spirit is a lamp of the Lord.

00:00:28.040 --> 00:00:31.320
So there is no need to envy the
magic lamp in Arabian tales.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:35.920
You and I are God’s lamps.
We have a spirit within us.

00:00:35.920 --> 00:00:40.620
The Bible describes human beings as vessels—

00:00:40.620 --> 00:00:45.560
containers made to hold
something rich and meaningful.

00:00:45.560 --> 00:00:50.560
But we are not like a soda bottle or a wine bottle.

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:54.000
A bottle has just one compartment.
Fill it, and it is full.

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:59.020
We have three dimensions: spirit, soul and body.

00:00:59.020 --> 00:01:03.700
The Bible presents itself as God speaking to us.

00:01:03.700 --> 00:01:08.460
It speaks about the past, the future, and who God is—

00:01:08.460 --> 00:01:12.140
and why we were created.

00:01:12.140 --> 00:01:17.340
The Creator has given us an
instruction manual for life.

00:01:17.340 --> 00:01:22.040
Searching on our own is not
enough. Turn to God’s words,

00:01:22.040 --> 00:01:24.860
and you begin to discover what life really means.

00:01:24.860 --> 00:01:32.820
After creating humanity, God placed
people in a garden in the east.

00:01:32.820 --> 00:01:39.300
Think of the east, where the
sun rises in the morning:

00:01:39.300 --> 00:01:43.440
a place of sunrise, hope and glory.

00:01:43.440 --> 00:01:48.460
God’s purpose for us is filled with hope and glory.

00:01:48.460 --> 00:01:52.700
That garden in the east is called Eden.

00:01:52.700 --> 00:01:58.920
Eden is a garden of joy, fulfillment and delight.

00:01:58.920 --> 00:02:04.560
God designed life for joy, not suffering.

00:02:04.560 --> 00:02:11.480
In the garden were two things,
presenting people with a choice.

00:02:11.480 --> 00:02:15.680
To put it simply, the garden had all kinds of trees

00:02:15.680 --> 00:02:17.860
to meet our physical needs.

00:02:17.860 --> 00:02:23.840
There was also beautiful
scenery, with flowers and trees—

00:02:23.840 --> 00:02:27.120
so much to delight our eyes and lift our hearts.

00:02:27.120 --> 00:02:31.160
But there was another tree: the tree of life.

00:02:31.160 --> 00:02:36.680
This is the key: the life represented by that tree.

00:02:36.680 --> 00:02:41.780
It is there at the beginning, in
Genesis. Throughout the Bible

00:02:41.780 --> 00:02:44.780
runs a path toward receiving this life.

00:02:44.780 --> 00:02:50.220
Then Jesus came and said
something that may sound puzzling.

00:02:50.220 --> 00:02:54.160
But once you experience it, it
becomes wonderfully meaningful.

00:02:54.160 --> 00:02:58.320
He said, “I have come that they may have life,

00:02:58.320 --> 00:03:01.320
and may have it abundantly.”

00:03:01.320 --> 00:03:05.880
Ultimately, this life continues
into the New Jerusalem.

00:03:05.880 --> 00:03:10.320
There, a river of the water of
life flows through the city,

00:03:10.320 --> 00:03:14.860
with the tree of life on either
side, sustaining us forever.

00:03:14.860 --> 00:03:18.020
The Bible says that God so loved the world

00:03:18.020 --> 00:03:20.760
that He gave His only begotten Son,

00:03:20.760 --> 00:03:25.760
that everyone who believes
into Him—“believe into Him”—

00:03:25.760 --> 00:03:31.000
would not perish, but would have eternal life.
